WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/components/feedback/SessionExpiredModal.tsx — the ForwardAuth "session fully expired" hard block.
    Hooks: useTranslation; useSessionMonitor() → { mode, hasExpired }. Local state: eventTriggered (set true by
    a `teslasync:session-expired` document CustomEvent — the "a 401 fired between polls" path; sticky once true).
    Branches:
      • mode === 'open'                 → return null (no auth provider; the event is ignored here too).
      • open = hasExpired || eventTriggered.
      • <Modal open onClose={no-op} size="sm" ariaLabel=t('session.expired.title','Session expired')> — NON-
        dismissible (Esc + backdrop are absorbed); the ONLY exit is the action.
        Body (space-y-4 text-center): rose lock disc (bg-rose-300/15 + Lock text-rose-300);
        h2 t('session.expired.title','Session expired'); p t('session.expired.body','For your security, your
        session has timed out. Sign in again to pick up where you left off.');
        <Button variant=primary className="w-full" onClick=handleSignIn>t('session.expired.signIn','Sign in
        again')</Button>.
      • handleSignIn → navigateToReauth() (lib/resilience) — explicit IdP handoff (writes current URL +
        embeds it in rd=); replaces the fragile reload-current-path behaviour behind a Service Worker.
    i18n keys extracted: session.expired.title, session.expired.body, session.expired.signIn.

NATIVE OUTPUT (apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/SessionExpiredModal.*)
  Adapter.swift    — pure projection core (Foundation only): surface slug, SessionMode/LoadStatus/Connection/
                     Phase, SessionContext (+ sticky-event latchingEvent), SessionExpiredProjection
                     (shouldBlock = web `open`; resolvePhase; resolved).
  Seams.swift      — P1/S11 telemetry seam (view.opened), re-auth control seam (web navigateToReauth),
                     coalesced source snapshot, P1/S8 SessionExpiredSource protocol + in-memory source,
                     P1/S10 i18n facade, VoiceOver summary builders.
  Model.swift      — @MainActor @Observable SessionExpiredModel (P1/S8): latches the 401 event, resolves
                     phase + freshness, drives signIn (web navigateToReauth), emits view.opened once,
                     guarded stale auto-refresh; isBlocking / isOffline derived.
  States.swift     — loading (skeleton chrome, shapes — no redaction-reason literal), empty (open mode),
                     dormant (healthy session), error (QueryError + retry), freshness chip, connectivity banner.
  Views.swift      — the expired hard block (web Modal body): rose lock disc, title, body, full-width
                     "Sign in again", offline note; + the i18n Text helper.
  SessionExpiredModal.swift — the View: TSFadeIn + TSGlassPanel, conditional freshness chip, switches over
                     phase; non-dismissible (no close affordance); onAppear start / onDisappear stop; a11y.
  Previews.swift   — one #Preview per state (Expired / Empty-open / Dormant / Loading / Error / Stale / Offline).
  SessionExpiredModal.strings — P1/S10 catalog: the 3 verbatim web keys + the native-envelope keys.
  Tests.swift / ModelTests.swift — adapter/projection/a11y + state-holder coverage (co-located XCTest).

STATE MAPPING (every prompt-required state renders — no hidden surface)
  loading  → phase .loading        : skeleton chrome (icon disc + title/body/action bars, reduce-motion-aware pulse)
  empty    → phase .empty          : open mode — "No sign-in required" ContentUnavailableView (web `return null`)
  error    → phase .error(msg)     : "Couldn't check your session" + Retry → model.refresh()
  stale    → connection .stale     : stale chip + one guarded auto-refresh (re-armed on return to live)
  offline  → connection .offline   : cached verdict kept + offline chip + banner + "reconnect to sign in" note
  content  → phase .expired        : THE hard block (web Modal body) — rose lock, title, body, full-width CTA
  (+ web)  → phase .dormant        : healthy session, block not engaged (web Modal open=false) shown as a
                                     reassuring "Session active" panel rather than a blank box
  Event latch: a `teslasync:session-expired` fold-in keeps .expired even if a later poll reports healthy
               (web sticky `eventTriggered`) — covered by a model test.

